{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3003","id":3162881059,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz8868hbwj","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3003","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3003.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3003.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3003","number":3003,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"OIDC: Add configurable username mapping via `oidc.username_claim_order`","user":{"login":"angelbarrera92","id":14357604,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzU3NjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14357604?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelbarrera92","html_url":"https://github.com/angelbarrera92","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelbarrera92/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelbarrera92/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelbarrera92/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelbarrera92/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelbarrera92/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelbarrera92/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelbarrera92/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelbarrera92/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelbarrera92/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Add support for deriving Headscale usernames from configurable OIDC claims, addressing IdPs (like Google) that omit the standard `preferred_username` claim.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nHeadscale is \"Open Source, acknowledged contribution\", this means that any\r\ncontribution will have to be discussed with the Maintainers before being submitted.\r\n\r\nThis model has been chosen to reduce the risk of burnout by limiting the\r\nmaintenance overhead of reviewing and validating third-party code.\r\n\r\nHeadscale is open to code contributions for bug fixes without discussion.\r\n\r\nIf you find mistakes in the documentation, please submit a fix to the documentation.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n<!-- Please tick if the following things apply. You… -->\r\n\r\n- [x] have read the [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) file\r\n- [x] raised a GitHub issue or discussed it on the projects chat beforehand\r\n- [x] added unit tests\r\n- [x] added integration tests\r\n- [x] updated documentation if needed\r\n- [ ] updated CHANGELOG.md\r\n\r\n<!-- If applicable, please reference the issue using `Fixes #XXX` and add tests to cover your new code. -->\r\n\r\nFixes #3002 \r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nThis PR adds a configurable way to derive the Headscale username from OIDC claims. It addresses IdPs (like Google) that do not emit `preferred_username`, enabling predictable, valid usernames without manual remediation.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- Config: Introduce `oidc.username_claim_order` (array) that defines a priority list of claims to try.\r\n  - Supported values: `preferred_username`, `email_localpart`, `email`, `name`, `sub`.\r\n  - Default (when unset): `[preferred_username, email_localpart, email, name, sub]`.\r\n- Username derivation helper: picks the first non-empty, syntactically valid candidate using existing `ValidateUsername` rules.\r\n- OIDC flow: applies the mapping before creating/updating the user record so `Username()` resolves reliably.\r\n- Documentation: added configuration reference and OIDC guide notes (including Google example).\r\n- Tests: unit tests covering the derivation and common fallback cases.\r\n\r\n## Example Configuration\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\noidc:\r\n  issuer: \"https://accounts.google.com\"\r\n  client_id: \"...\"\r\n  client_secret: \"...\"\r\n  # Prefer preferred_username, otherwise use email local-part, then email\r\n  username_claim_order:\r\n    - preferred_username\r\n    - email_localpart\r\n    - email\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\n- Candidates are tried in order and must pass `ValidateUsername`.\r\n- If the list is omitted, the default order is used.\r\n- Default behavior preserves existing installs where `preferred_username` is present.\r\n- No database migrations required.\r\n- Username syntax is validated; all email verification and authorization constraints remain unchanged.\r\n","created_at":"2026-01-11T06:26:00Z","updated_at":"2026-01-11T06:26:17Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock","html_url":"https://github.com/nblock","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.